          "  // INITIAL LOAD\n  const onInitialLoad = useEffectEvent(() => {\n    loadChats();\n  });\n  useEffect(() => {\n    onInitialLoad();\n  }, []);",
          "  // Auto-save when generation completes\n  // Changes whenever the message count, last message id or its generating flag\n  // changes; null while the last message is still generating\n  const settledChatKey = lastMessageInHistory?.isGenerating\n    ? null\n    : JSON.stringify([\n        chatHistory.messages?.length,\n        lastMessageInHistory?.id,\n        lastMessageInHistory?.isGenerating,\n      ]);\n  const onChatSettled = useEffectEvent(() => {\n    saveCurrentChat();\n  });\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (settledChatKey !== null) {\n      onChatSettled();\n    }\n  }, [settledChatKey]);"
        ],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed all four issues in `useTTDChatStorage.ts`. I couldn't re-run the linter: there's no `node_modules` in the project, and the commands to look for an installed `oxlint` needed approval, which this run can't get. So the fix hasn't been checked by a lint run yet.\n\n**Issues 1 and 3 (initial-load effect, line 186):** the effect should run once on mount, not every time `loadChats` changes (it changes whenever `isLoading` or `chatsLoaded` flips). I moved the call into an effect event, `onInitialLoad`, made with `useEffectEvent` (the project is on React 19.3). The effect calls `onInitialLoad()` and keeps its empty `[]` list. It still loads once on mount using the current `loadChats`. It also won't start reloading if something else resets the exported `chatsLoadedAtom`, which simply adding `loadChats` to the list would have caused.\n\n**Issues 2 and 4 (auto-save effect, line 254):**\n- **Missing `saveCurrentChat`:** adding it to the list would have changed behaviour. It changes whenever anything in `chatHistory` changes, such as `currentPrompt`, so the effect would have saved to storage far more often. It's now called through an effect event, `onChatSettled`, so it no longer counts as a dependency.\n- **\"Unnecessary\" message count and last message id:** these are the real triggers for the save, but the effect body never read them. I combined them, with the last message's generating flag, into one value in render, `settledChatKey`. It's `null` while the last message is still generating. The effect now depends only on `settledChatKey` and checks it in its body.\n\nIt saves in the same cases as before: on mount, and whenever the message count, last message id or generating flag changes, as long as the last message isn't still generating.",
